    "rationale": "Hemoconcentration in preeclampsia results from capillary leakage due to endothelial damage, causing fluid shift out of the intravascular space and into tissues, manifesting as edema of the face and hands, alongside thrombocytopenia (from platelet and fibrin deposition) and microangiopathic hemolysis (from RBC breakdown).",
