    "stem": "A 54-year-old postmenopausal woman complains of severe vaginal dryness, burning, and recurrent urinary tract infections. She has absolutely no hot flashes or night sweats. Her past medical history includes a deep vein thrombosis (DVT) 10 years ago after knee surgery. Her physician diagnoses Genitourinary Syndrome of Menopause (vaginal atrophy). Which of the following is the safest and most effective pharmacologic treatment for this patient's specific symptoms?",
