    "stem": "A 55-year-old woman presents to the clinic with mixed urinary incontinence. She leaks urine when she sneezes (Stress incontinence) and also has sudden, overwhelming urges to run to the bathroom (Urge incontinence). The physician decides to start her on Imipramine, a tricyclic antidepressant (TCA), which has been shown to be uniquely effective in treating mixed incontinence. What dual mechanism of action makes Imipramine effective for both types of incontinence simultaneously?",
