    "topic": "Lecture 5.1: Lower Genital Tract Diseases - Set 2",
    "yield_level": "Mid",
    "stem": "A 34-year-old woman has a Pap smear showing atypical squamous cells of undetermined significance (ASC-US). Because this is a borderline, ambiguous result, the physician orders reflex HPV DNA testing on the same sample to determine the next step in management. The test returns positive for a high-risk HPV strain. Which of the following high-risk strains is the most common cause of cervical cancer worldwide?",
