    "stem": "A 45-year-old woman undergoes a total hysterectomy (removal of both the uterus and cervix) for symptomatic, benign uterine fibroids. She has a history of normal Pap smears and has never had cervical dysplasia or HPV. She asks her physician if she still needs to come in for her routine Pap smears now that her uterus is gone. Which of the following is the most appropriate advice according to current guidelines?",
