    "stem": "A 60-year-old woman undergoes a hysterectomy for a rapidly enlarging, fleshy uterine mass. The gross specimen reveals a bulky, poorly demarcated mass with extensive areas of hemorrhage and yellow-gray necrosis. The pathologist must confirm the diagnosis of Leiomyosarcoma microscopically. Which of the following histologic features is an absolute requirement to make this malignant diagnosis?",
