    "rationale": "Leiomyosarcoma is a rare tumor typically occurring in older patients (50-60 years), presenting with abnormal bleeding and a poor prognosis, often with lymph node invasion. Histology shows necrosis, increased mitotic count, and cytologic atypia, distinguishing it from benign leiomyoma.",
